    description: 'A full-stack BI app (FastAPI + React 19). Most of the work went into measuring whether the LLM output is any good. Nine canonical pipeline stages each record duration, model, prompt version, attempts and token usage to a job_stages table, and carry two independent quality scores: a deterministic completeness score against a per-stage contract, and an optional LLM critic confidence score that triggers a targeted re-run below threshold. The agent runtime replaces six duplicated agent classes with one spec plus a runner whose retry ladder distinguishes parse failures (repair turn feeding back the raw output and error) from transport failures (backoff with jitter). Progress streams over SSE with a polling fallback serving the identical payload, so a mid-run refresh reconstructs the full timeline. An offline eval harness runs seven saved fixtures (including a government site as a hallucination canary) and fails on regression. It also has an SSRF guard that re-validates every redirect, Upstash-backed rate limiting, and a five-provider email registry that raises at startup on misconfiguration so mail is never dropped silently.',
